# S8 — strand-agnostic (canonical) k-mer spectrum, k=10, over the 10 Mbp genome.
# A k-mer and its reverse complement collapse to one entry (the lexicographically
# smaller). `canonical_kmer_counts` does it natively on the 2-bit-packed code
# (complement = bits XOR 3, then reversed) — one method vs everyone else's loop.
seq = read_fasta("data/genome.fa")[0].seq
counts = seq.canonical_kmer_counts(10)
vals = counts.map((kmer, c) => c)
print("distinct={counts.count()}")
print("total={vals.sum()}")
print("max={vals.reduce(0, (a, x) => if x > a then x else a)}")
